jobs.description:
**About The Role**
Lift Schools is looking for an internal communications and policy manager to shape how we connect, inform and inspire colleagues across our national network of 62 schools.


This is a chance to create the internal communications strategy that keeps our central teams, regional colleagues and school leaders informed, engaged and connected. You'll craft the messaging that matters – from trust-wide campaigns to complex policy updates – and make sure it reaches the right people in the right way.


You'll look after our core internal channels, including staff and principal newsletters, weekly briefings and our intranet. You'll also translate education policy into clear, actionable briefings that help senior leaders make informed decisions. This is a role where your words will strengthen our culture, support retention and help every colleague feel part of something bigger.


Key responsibilities


**You Will**

* shape our internal communications strategy and create messaging frameworks that keep colleagues across schools, central and regional teams informed and engaged;
* create, edit and publish written and visual content for staff newsletters, weekly briefings and intranet articles;
* support leadership communications by helping the CEO and executive team share priority messages effectively across the network;
* monitor education policy developments, DfE announcements and sector updates, and turn complex information into clear briefings for senior leaders and staff;
* regularly evaluate how well our channels are working, and identify new ways to reach different colleague groups; and
* manage the internal communications calendar to balance priorities and meet publication deadlines.

What we're looking for


**You Will Bring**

* at least three years' experience in internal communications, corporate communications or policy communications within a complex, multi-site organisation;
* exceptional copywriting and editing skills across digital and print formats, with the ability to tailor content for different audiences;
* a background managing and improving internal digital channels like intranets, newsletters and digital platforms;
* a strong understanding of how communications supports colleague engagement, culture and retention;
* the ability to use audience feedback and engagement data to evaluate what's working and continuously improve; and
* a strong understanding of UK education policy, or the ability to quickly grasp it and translate updates into engaging content for staff.

You'll be a confident storyteller who can build trusted relationships at all levels. You'll manage multiple priorities with care, meet deadlines, and bring a proactive approach to improving how we communicate. Can you create clarity from complexity and help colleagues feel truly connected to our mission?


Regular travel between schools is required, so you'll need a full UK driving licence and access to a vehicle. Mileage for travel between schools during the working day will be reimbursed from your base location.


Who is Lift Schools?


Lift Schools is made up of 62 primary, secondary and special schools, educating more than 35,000 pupils across the country. We believe education can transform lives – and we want every child in our schools to achieve their full potential.


How we support you


We want you to feel supported, valued and able to grow throughout your career with Lift Schools. From high-quality professional development and career progression to wellbeing support and opportunities to connect and collaborate across our network, we invest in you so you can do your best work. Discover how we'll support you to thrive, develop and grow your career in the way that's right for you: How we support you.
